under vendor/ and crates/ghostty-vt keep their own licenses.

Summary of modifications made in flockr (see `git log` for the exact changes):

1. Rename. The product, crate, binary, config and state directories
   (`~/.config/flockr`, `flockr-dev` for debug builds), socket and log file names,
   CLI output and UI text, `TERM_PROGRAM`, `FLOCKR_*` environment variables,
   `flockr:<id>` agent report sources, integration hook script names and markers,
   plugin manifest (`flockr-plugin.toml`, `min_flockr_version`), remote bridge
   markers, and config values (`ui.toast.delivery = "flockr"`,
   `[ui.toast.flockr]`, `--right-click flockr`) were renamed from herdr.
2. Compatibility layer (`src/legacy_herdr.rs`). Panes also export the legacy
   `HERDR_*` variables; env vars read by the server and CLI fall back from
   `FLOCKR_*` to `HERDR_*` (except instance identity variables); `herdr:<id>`
   report sources are accepted as aliases of `flockr:<id>`; the old `"herdr"`
   config and CLI values are accepted as deprecated aliases. `~/.config/herdr`
   is never read or migrated.
3. Hosting. Self-update, release notes, product announcements, remote installer
   downloads and agent-detection manifest fetches point at
   https://github.com/Rambarani/flockr (constants in `src/product.rs`) instead of
   herdr.dev and the upstream GitHub repository.
4. Feature: sidebar agents are grouped under workspace headers.
5. Feature: configurable notification sounds with built-in tones and a settings
   picker.
